# Windows batch files must keep CRLF line endings.
#
# cmd.exe mis-executes a .bat that uses bare LF: it reads fragments of comment
# lines as commands. Editing bbpull.cmd with a tool that normalises to LF broke
# the launcher exactly that way, and it is not obvious from reading the file.
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine would otherwise rewrite them on checkout.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Python sources stay LF.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
